<title>USA: Ga. $35 mln housing bonds repriced, restructured.</title>
<headline>Ga. $35 mln housing bonds repriced, restructured.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc said Thursday it repriced and restructured Georgia Housing and Finance Authority's $35 million mortgage bonds, raising the top yield in 2028 to 6.15 percent from 6.125 percent and lowering the 2019 maturity to 5.60 percent from 5.65 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>GEORGIA HOUSING AND FINANCE AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $35,000,000*</p>
<p>SINGLE FAMILY MORTGAGE BONDS</p>
<p>1996 SERIES B</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD. THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED.</p>
<p>NOTE THE REPRICING.</p>
<p>					     4,860,000*</p>
<p>				    SUBSERIES B-1 (NON-AMT)</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aa		    S&amp;P: AA+</p>
<p>    DATED: 10/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 06/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
